What is UCO Biodiesel?
UCO Biodiesel is a sustainable fuel produced from Used Cooking Oil (UCO), a type of waste vegetable oil. Through a chemical process called transesterification, the triglycerides present in the used cooking oil are converted into Fatty Acid Methyl Esters (FAME). This biofuel stands as a renewable and environmentally responsible alternative to conventional diesel, as it not only helps in reducing waste but also significantly lowers greenhouse gas emissions, contributing to a cleaner environment.
Recognized for its role in the circular economy, UCO Biodiesel is gaining substantial traction across various regions, supported by government mandates and incentives aimed at promoting cleaner energy sources and reducing dependency on fossil fuels.
